    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "HO3 requires discovering and reconciling non-opening, case-specific hidden context such as prior childhood fainting episodes, the exact discharge diagnosis wording, or unclear tilt-related testing. The doctor retrieved workspace records that contained prior syncope history and discharge diagnosis, but this was a routine clinical query to gather standard history; the doctor did not actively elicit or integrate a new hidden fact that materially contextualized follow-up beyond the minimum Holter-closure requirement. No distinct beyond-minimum discovery was made.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "HO4 requires identifying a specific caregiver misconception, giving a plain-language correction, and linking it to a concrete behavior. The family did not surface a clear misconception such as '体位性低血压/心动过快' or 'no further fainting means nothing'. The doctor corrected the general misunderstanding that POTS excludes cardiac risk, but this was part of the standard RC3/RC7 non-overreach boundary, not a targeted correction of a specific family misconception. No distinct HO4 completion occurred.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    }
  ],
